+// set first, before any other step or return (the policy hook G2 reads it inside the decline; gin-restore's contract).
+// New (EXPERIMENT.md 9.1 (g)): a loss while waiting for DONE first gets the idle loop's liveness verdict (gdakiTsCauseLiveness
+// on the receive's cause), without that loop's side effects. Dead (a FIN without BYE, BADMAGIC, an errno outside the unknown
+// list): the peer is judged dead through gdakiTsSocketLost (the idle loop's two lines, the death count, the socket closed,
+// gone) and declined with cause PeerDead and GDAKI_UA_PEER_DEAD, so the communicator degrades NCCL_GIN_TS_DEGRADED_MS later
+// as after any death. hw declined with Unknown and DECLINED: no degraded raise, and with three or more ranks this rank's
+// waits that name no peer stayed held, while the other survivors judged the same death from their own sockets. Anything
+// else (unknown: a reset, a timeout; after the peer's BYE) is declined as in hw (gone, cause Unknown); the unknown verdict is
+// not handed to the reconnect machinery (a declined peer is never re-dialed).
+// A failed ACK send takes no death verdict: a send fails with an error only after the connection was reset or timed out
+// (unknown), or for this rank's own socket state, while a peer's FIN alone leaves the socket writable. The send's errno is
+// named into pe.closeCause (gdakiTsSend writes none; as hw does at its other send failures) and the receive side is not
+// peeked: the failed send consumed the socket error, so a peek would read a reset as a FIN (review of hk, finding 1).
+static void gdakiTsDeclineAfterCommit(struct gdakiRecHost* r, int peer, uint64_t round, const char* what, int cls,
